# Cursor Rules for iOS Dashboard Project

## Project Context
This is a premium iOS/visionOS-style vertical dashboard built with Next.js + Tauri for Windows desktop.
It features glassmorphism UI, real-time hardware monitoring via Rust backend, and an AI assistant dock.

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4
- Desktop: Tauri v2 with Rust backend
- UI: shadcn/ui components + custom glassmorphism design system

## Code Style

### TypeScript/React
- Use "use client" directive for components with hooks or browser APIs
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use `cn()` from `lib/utils` for conditional class merging
- Always handle hydration: use `mounted` state for time/date displays

### Tailwind CSS v4
- NO tailwind.config.ts - all config in `app/globals.css` under `@theme inline`
- Use semantic tokens: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`
- Custom classes: `.glass-card`, `.dock-glass`, `.neon-progress`
- Prefer gap over margin for spacing in flex/grid

### Tauri Integration
- All system commands defined in `src-tauri/src/main.rs`
- Frontend uses `lib/tauri.ts` for type-safe invoke wrapper
- Always check `isTauri()` before calling Tauri APIs
- Provide fallback/demo data for web preview

### Rust Backend
- Use sysinfo crate for CPU/RAM monitoring
- Use nvml-wrapper for NVIDIA GPU (with error handling fallback)
- Return serializable structs with serde

## File Locations
- Dashboard widgets: `components/dashboard/`
- Tauri types/helpers: `lib/tauri.ts`
- Global styles: `app/globals.css`
- Rust backend: `src-tauri/src/main.rs`

## Design Guidelines
- Glassmorphism: backdrop-blur + translucent bg + thin white border
- Colors: Deep dark blues/purples, white text, neon accents
- Animations: Subtle hover effects, smooth transitions (300ms)
- Border radius: 24px for cards, 16px for buttons
- Mobile-first: 420px width, vertical scroll layout

## Common Patterns

### Adding a new widget
1. Create component in `components/dashboard/`
2. Use `.glass-card` class for container
3. Add to `app/page.tsx` in the flex column

### Adding Tauri command
1. Add command function in `src-tauri/src/main.rs`
2. Register in `.invoke_handler(tauri::generate_handler![...])`
3. Add TypeScript types in `lib/tauri.ts`
4. Use `invokeTauri<T>()` wrapper in component

### Styling new elements
1. Check existing design tokens in `globals.css`
2. Use semantic classes when possible
3. Add new custom classes in globals.css if reusable
